{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01X2YrdkAGLDv4Sotsh68F7q","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation Plan: Measure-Enhance-Measure Automation\n2\t\n3\t**Branch**: `003-eval-automation` | **Date**: 2026-05-27 | **Spec**: [spec.md](spec.md)\n4\t**Input**: Feature specification from `specs/003-eval-automation/spec.md`\n5\t\n6\t## Summary\n7\t\n8\tAdd a `skill:measure` skill and a `scripts/compare-runs.sh` script to cc-skill. The skill orchestrates the baseline-enhance-reeval loop within a single Claude Code session. The script computes deterministic comparison deltas between two eval runs, producing both terminal output and a markdown report.\n9\t\n10\t## Technical Context\n11\t\n12\t**Language/Version**: Bash (script), Markdown (SKILL.md)\n13\t**Primary Dependencies**: yq (YAML parsing), agent-eval-harness plugin (eval-run skill)\n14\t**Storage**: N/A (reads existing eval run directories)\n15\t**Testing**: Manual testing against real eval runs\n16\t**Target Platform**: macOS/Linux (Claude Code environments)\n17\t**Project Type**: Claude Code plugin (new skill + utility script)\n18\t**Constraints**: No nested claude -p sessions (FR-013), script must be standalone (FR-010)\n19\t\n20\t## Constitution Check\n21\t\n22\t*GATE: Must pass before Phase 0 research. Re-check after Phase 1 design.*\n23\t\n24\tConstitution is a blank template. No gates to evaluate. Passes by default.\n25\t\n26\t## Project Structure\n27\t\n28\t### Documentation (this feature)\n29\t\n30\t```text\n31\tspecs/003-eval-automation/\n32\t├── spec.md              # Feature specification\n33\t├── plan.md              # This file\n34\t├── research.md          # Phase 0: summary.yaml format, scoring logic\n35\t└── tasks.md             # Phase 2 output (created by /speckit-tasks)\n36\t```\n37\t\n38\t### Source Code (repository root)\n39\t\n40\t```text\n41\tskill/\n42\t├── skills/\n43\t│   ├── checker/\n44\t│   │   └── SKILL.md           # Existing\n45\t│   ├── enhancer/\n46\t│   │   └── SKILL.md           # Existing\n47\t│   └── measure/\n48\t│       └── SKILL.md           # NEW: skill:measure orchestration skill\n49\t└── scripts/\n50\t    └── compare-runs.sh        # NEW: deterministic comparison script\n51\t```\n52\t\n53\t**Structure Decision**: Two new files in the existing plugin structure. The skill goes in `skill/skills/measure/SKILL.md` following the existing pattern (checker, enhancer). The script goes in `skill/scripts/` since it's a utility bundled with the plugin.\n54\t\n55\t## Design Decisions\n56\t\n57\t### D1: Skill Architecture\n58\t\n59\t`skill:measure` is an orchestration skill. It invokes three other skills in sequence:\n60\t1. `/eval-run` (from agent-eval-harness) for baseline\n61\t2. `/skill:enhance` (from this plugin) for enhancement\n62\t3. `/eval-run` (from agent-eval-harness) for re-evaluation\n63\t\n64\tAfter both eval runs, it calls `scripts/compare-runs.sh` via Bash with the two run directory paths.\n65\t\n66\tThe skill does not duplicate any eval logic. It's pure orchestration.\n67\t\n68\t### D2: Comparison Script Design\n69\t\n70\t`compare-runs.sh` takes two positional arguments (run directory paths), reads `summary.yaml` from each, and:\n71\t1. Extracts all judge names from both files (union set)\n72\t2. For each judge, reads `mean` (numeric) or `pass_rate` (boolean)\n73\t3. Computes delta (enhanced - baseline)\n74\t4. Prints a formatted table to stdout\n75\t5. Writes a detailed markdown report to `<run-dir-2>/comparison.md`\n76\t\n77\tUses `yq` for YAML parsing. No Python dependency.\n78\t\n79\t### D3: Already-Optimal Detection\n80\t\n81\tWhen `/skill:enhance` reports a skill is already optimal (all patterns strong), `skill:measure` skips the re-evaluation step and reports \"no enhancement needed.\" This avoids a wasted eval run that would produce identical scores.\n82\t\n83\tThe skill detects this by reading skill:enhance's conversation output for the \"already optimal\" signal.\n84\t\n85\t### D4: Error Handling\n86\t\n87\t- Missing eval.yaml: skill:measure checks for eval.yaml before starting and directs user to `/eval-analyze`\n88\t- Missing summary.yaml: compare-runs.sh validates both directories and exits with a clear error\n89\t- Mismatched judges: compare-runs.sh shows N/A for judges present in only one run\n90\t- Interrupted loop: skill:measure reports what completed (e.g., \"baseline complete, enhancement failed\")\n91\t\n92\t### D5: summary.yaml Contract\n93\t\n94\tThe comparison script depends on this structure from the eval-harness:\n95\t\n96\t```yaml\n97\tjudges:\n98\t  judge_name:\n99\t    mean: 4.2        # float or null (numeric judges)\n100\t    pass_rate: 0.85   # float or null (boolean judges)\n101\t```\n102\t\n103\tFor each judge, the script uses `pass_rate` if non-null, otherwise `mean`. This handles both boolean and numeric judges uniformly.\n104\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ca317b90-dcab-4e94-97cd-6de7e52b3cf4","uuid":"c67d343c-5b44-47ad-a688-051490f77347","timestamp":"2026-06-01T15:27:55.299Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/rhuss/Development/context-engineering/cc-skill/specs/003-eval-automation/plan.md","content":"# Implementation Plan: Measure-Enhance-Measure Automation\n\n**Branch**: `003-eval-automation` | **Date**: 2026-05-27 | **Spec**: [spec.md](spec.md)\n**Input**: Feature specification from `specs/003-eval-automation/spec.md`\n\n## Summary\n\nAdd a `skill:measure` skill and a `scripts/compare-runs.sh` script to cc-skill. The skill orchestrates the baseline-enhance-reeval loop within a single Claude Code session. The script computes deterministic comparison deltas between two eval runs, producing both terminal output and a markdown report.\n\n## Technical Context\n\n**Language/Version**: Bash (script), Markdown (SKILL.md)\n**Primary Dependencies**: yq (YAML parsing), agent-eval-harness plugin (eval-run skill)\n**Storage**: N/A (reads existing eval run directories)\n**Testing**: Manual testing against real eval runs\n**Target Platform**: macOS/Linux (Claude Code environments)\n**Project Type**: Claude Code plugin (new skill + utility script)\n**Constraints**: No nested claude -p sessions (FR-013), script must be standalone (FR-010)\n\n## Constitution Check\n\n*GATE: Must pass before Phase 0 research. Re-check after Phase 1 design.*\n\nConstitution is a blank template. No gates to evaluate. Passes by default.\n\n## Project Structure\n\n### Documentation (this feature)\n\n```text\nspecs/003-eval-automation/\n├── spec.md              # Feature specification\n├── plan.md              # This file\n├── research.md          # Phase 0: summary.yaml format, scoring logic\n└── tasks.md             # Phase 2 output (created by /speckit-tasks)\n```\n\n### Source Code (repository root)\n\n```text\nskill/\n├── skills/\n│   ├── checker/\n│   │   └── SKILL.md           # Existing\n│   ├── enhancer/\n│   │   └── SKILL.md           # Existing\n│   └── measure/\n│       └── SKILL.md           # NEW: skill:measure orchestration skill\n└── scripts/\n    └── compare-runs.sh        # NEW: deterministic comparison script\n```\n\n**Structure Decision**: Two new files in the existing plugin structure. The skill goes in `skill/skills/measure/SKILL.md` following the existing pattern (checker, enhancer). The script goes in `skill/scripts/` since it's a utility bundled with the plugin.\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### D1: Skill Architecture\n\n`skill:measure` is an orchestration skill. It invokes three other skills in sequence:\n1. `/eval-run` (from agent-eval-harness) for baseline\n2. `/skill:enhance` (from this plugin) for enhancement\n3. `/eval-run` (from agent-eval-harness) for re-evaluation\n\nAfter both eval runs, it calls `scripts/compare-runs.sh` via Bash with the two run directory paths.\n\nThe skill does not duplicate any eval logic. It's pure orchestration.\n\n### D2: Comparison Script Design\n\n`compare-runs.sh` takes two positional arguments (run directory paths), reads `summary.yaml` from each, and:\n1. Extracts all judge names from both files (union set)\n2. For each judge, reads `mean` (numeric) or `pass_rate` (boolean)\n3. Computes delta (enhanced - baseline)\n4. Prints a formatted table to stdout\n5. Writes a detailed markdown report to `<run-dir-2>/comparison.md`\n\nUses `yq` for YAML parsing. No Python dependency.\n\n### D3: Already-Optimal Detection\n\nWhen `/skill:enhance` reports a skill is already optimal (all patterns strong), `skill:measure` skips the re-evaluation step and reports \"no enhancement needed.\" This avoids a wasted eval run that would produce identical scores.\n\nThe skill detects this by reading skill:enhance's conversation output for the \"already optimal\" signal.\n\n### D4: Error Handling\n\n- Missing eval.yaml: skill:measure checks for eval.yaml before starting and directs user to `/eval-analyze`\n- Missing summary.yaml: compare-runs.sh validates both directories and exits with a clear error\n- Mismatched judges: compare-runs.sh shows N/A for judges present in only one run\n- Interrupted loop: skill:measure reports what completed (e.g., \"baseline complete, enhancement failed\")\n\n### D5: summary.yaml Contract\n\nThe comparison script depends on this structure from the eval-harness:\n\n```yaml\njudges:\n  judge_name:\n    mean: 4.2        # float or null (numeric judges)\n    pass_rate: 0.85   # float or null (boolean judges)\n```\n\nFor each judge, the script uses `pass_rate` if non-null, otherwise `mean`. This handles both boolean and numeric judges uniformly.\n","numLines":104,"startLine":1,"totalLines":104}}}
